<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  bridge-cyclonedds.xml — the DDS side of the Mac's bridge.

  Not a template: nothing here is per-host. `scripts/install-bridge.sh` copies it
  to ~/.config/fm-comms/cyclonedds.xml on macOS and the LaunchAgent points
  CYCLONEDDS_URI at it.

  Why fm-comms carries a DDS config at all, when the ROS environment is fm-ros2's
  business: the bridge is this repo's process, started by this repo's LaunchAgent,
  and launchd sources no shell profile. It never reads comms-zenoh.sh, so the
  settings that profile exports reach every ROS node on the Mac and not the one
  process that has to join them. The values below are deliberately the same as
  that profile's, because the bridge and the nodes must land in the same graph.

  On a rig the same settings arrive through the shell the systemd unit inherits
  from the container image, which is why there is no Linux copy of this file.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <!-- Loopback has no multicast. Say so, rather than letting Cyclone
           discover it and log a warning on every start. -->
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <!-- What replaces multicast: probe localhost for peers. -->
      <Peers>
        <Peer address="localhost"/>
      </Peers>
      <!-- The ceiling that matters. Unicast discovery needs a distinct
           participant index per process and the default ceiling is nine — well
           under what a cockpit reaches once rviz, a foxglove bridge, and a
           handful of `ros2` commands are running. The tenth participant does not
           degrade, it fails outright:

             Failed to find a free participant index for domain 0

           and if the one that fails is this bridge, the Mac sees nothing from
           the fleet while every other process looks healthy. -->
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>60</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
